{
  "_comment": "The ViperAce ICP's DED screen. A 200x64 1-bit framebuffer driven over report 0xf0 (docs/PROTOCOL.md, \"Driving a pixel display\"). A bit index is a pixel, y*200+x, so the display is the same kind of map as the UFC's: each cell is the pixels of its box, generated from `grid`, and a glyph is the pixels it lights, drawn as rows of # in `fonts`.",
  "_source": "Geometry and the captured glyphs come from SimAppPro driving the ICP in a live F-16 mission, 2026-09-18, paired with the DCS-BIOS text sent during the same flight: crates/dsc-config/tests/fixtures/ded_simapppro_frames.txt and ded_bios_timeline.txt. The character set is SimAppPro's, from config/ICP/textfont_config_new.json.",
  "_status": "CONFIRMED on hardware 2026-09-18: the protocol, the grid and the captured glyphs. A page painted from this map matches SimAppPro's own frames byte for byte (tests/ded_render.rs). FLOWN 2026-09-18: the daemon drove the DED from DCS-BIOS in a live F-16, and every page tried (CNI, LIST, MISC, HMCS, TCN, IFF) drew correctly, inverse fields included. The drawn glyphs that did not appear on those pages have still not been on the glass.",
  "_notes": [
    "Captured, exactly as SimAppPro sent them: ABCDEFGHILMNOPQRSTUVX1234567890a()*o.: and space. '*' was only ever seen inverse and is that cell flipped back.",
    "Drawn here in the same style, not yet seen from SimAppPro: JKWYZ<>[]+-/=|du,!?;&_'\"%#@. Replace any of them with a capture when one turns up.",
    "DCS-BIOS spells some DED symbols as lowercase letters: 'a' is the up-and-down arrow and 'o' the degree sign, both captured. 'u' and 'd' are drawn as the up and down halves of 'a', which is a guess at what they stand for. Hence exact_case: uppercasing first would draw 'A' for the arrow.",
    "Inverse is drawn by the host, not the device: the cell's rows 1 to 11 are filled and the glyph knocked out of them. That is how SimAppPro draws the selected fields on the TCN page, and drawing DED_L3 with its format that way reproduces its frame byte for byte. A line's DED_Ln_FORMAT marks inverse characters with 'i'. 'b', big, is not drawn differently.",
    "Five lines of 24 characters on a 13 pixel pitch. Glyph ink sits in rows 2 to 10 of a cell and columns 1 to 6, so neighbouring characters never touch."
  ],
